WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.281
Welcome to The Fantastical Logic Grid.

2
00:00:03.431 --> 00:00:07.570
Every case is a brand new story, and you are
the detective.

3
00:00:08.370 --> 00:00:11.955
Each puzzle is a logic grid wrapped in a
story.

4
00:00:12.105 --> 00:00:15.654
The story sets up a mystery, the clues give
you the facts,

5
00:00:15.674 --> 00:00:18.655
and the grid is where you work out the answer.

6
00:00:19.455 --> 00:00:23.317
Every story is written fresh for you and never
repeated.

7
00:00:23.467 --> 00:00:28.289
And every puzzle has exactly one answer you
can reach without guessing.

8
00:00:29.089 --> 00:00:30.753
Here's how to play.

9
00:00:31.589 --> 00:00:35.216
Start on the New puzzle screen and pick a
difficulty.

10
00:00:35.366 --> 00:00:38.503
Basic and Easy are perfect for beginners.

11
00:00:38.653 --> 00:00:41.043
MENSA is for true masterminds.

12
00:00:41.843 --> 00:00:45.700
Next, choose a theme, like Mystery, Fantasy,
Sci-Fi,

13
00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:49.822
Around Town, National Parks or Vacation
Destinations.

14
00:00:49.972 --> 00:00:51.765
Or pick Surprise me.

15
00:00:52.565 --> 00:00:57.984
Most themes also have topics, like which
holiday or which kind of mystery.

16
00:00:58.134 --> 00:01:00.183
Pick one, or leave it on Any.

17
00:01:00.983 --> 00:01:02.583
Then pick a size.

18
00:01:02.733 --> 00:01:06.809
More categories and more items make a bigger,
harder grid.

19
00:01:07.609 --> 00:01:11.257
Full experience adds scenes, characters and
sound.

20
00:01:11.407 --> 00:01:16.528
Silent mode keeps only the story, the grid,
the clues and the answer key.

21
00:01:17.328 --> 00:01:21.510
Press Generate puzzle, and your story is
written in a moment.

22
00:01:22.310 --> 00:01:24.764
Here's our case: The Spooky Keys.

23
00:01:24.914 --> 00:01:27.901
The buttons along the top help you as you
play.

24
00:01:28.701 --> 00:01:30.515
Read the story first.

25
00:01:30.665 --> 00:01:35.850
It tells you who is involved, and it ends with
the question you need to answer.

26
00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:39.563
Here, it's: Who arrived at 9:45 PM?

27
00:01:39.713 --> 00:01:43.085
You can also press Read the story aloud to
hear it.

28
00:01:43.885 --> 00:01:47.768
Select a character's portrait to hear the
clues they remember.

29
00:01:47.918 --> 00:01:50.649
Every clue is also in the clue list.

30
00:01:51.449 --> 00:01:55.311
To hear every clue in order, press Read the
clues aloud.

31
00:01:55.461 --> 00:02:00.049
Each character tells their own clue, and the
clue being read lights up.

32
00:02:00.849 --> 00:02:06.631
On your first Easy puzzle, coach tips appear
above the grid to guide your first moves.

33
00:02:07.431 --> 00:02:08.797
Now the grid.

34
00:02:08.947 --> 00:02:13.939
Each square is where two things meet, like a
ghost hunter and an arrival time.

35
00:02:14.089 --> 00:02:17.439
Your job is to decide whether they go
together.

36
00:02:18.239 --> 00:02:21.099
Click or tap a square once to mark an X.

37
00:02:21.249 --> 00:02:24.791
X means ruled out: these two don't go
together.

38
00:02:25.591 --> 00:02:29.965
Tap again for an O. O means confirmed: these
two are a match.

39
00:02:30.115 --> 00:02:32.483
Tap a third time to clear the square.

40
00:02:33.283 --> 00:02:37.124
Let's solve it together, starting with the
simplest clues.

41
00:02:37.274 --> 00:02:43.760
Clue 1 says the ghost hunter who carried the
Flashlight arrived at 10:00 PM.

42
00:02:43.910 --> 00:02:45.361
Mark an O there.

43
00:02:46.161 --> 00:02:49.682
Clues 2 and 3 each rule out pairs directly.

44
00:02:49.832 --> 00:02:51.795
Mark an X for each one.

45
00:02:52.595 --> 00:02:57.715
Clue 4 says the ghost hunter who carried the
Flashlight is Felix or Hugo,

46
00:02:57.735 --> 00:03:00.489
so no other ghost hunter is possible.

47
00:03:01.289 --> 00:03:08.437
Clue 5 says the ghost hunter who carried the
Thermometer did not arrive at 9:30 PM.

48
00:03:08.587 --> 00:03:10.166
Mark an X there.

49
00:03:10.966 --> 00:03:15.127
Clue 6 says Felix arrived at 9:45 PM.

50
00:03:15.277 --> 00:03:16.728
Mark an O there.

51
00:03:17.528 --> 00:03:24.547
Clue 7 says the ghost hunter who carried the
Compass did not arrive at 9:45 PM.

52
00:03:24.697 --> 00:03:26.277
Mark an X there.

53
00:03:27.077 --> 00:03:33.903
Felix arrived at 9:45 PM, so Felix cannot go
with any other arrival,

54
00:03:33.923 --> 00:03:38.704
and no other ghost hunter can go with 9:45 PM.

55
00:03:38.854 --> 00:03:43.212
Each row and each column in a section has
exactly one match,

56
00:03:43.232 --> 00:03:46.300
so everything else in that line is an X.

57
00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:52.804
The ghost hunter who carried the Flashlight
arrived at 10:00 PM,

58
00:03:52.824 --> 00:04:00.754
so Flashlight cannot go with any other
arrival, and no other gear can go with 10:00
PM.

59
00:04:01.554 --> 00:04:06.099
9:15 PM is the only arrival left for
Thermometer.

60
00:04:06.249 --> 00:04:07.700
Mark an O there.

61
00:04:07.850 --> 00:04:12.885
When only one square is left in a row or
column, it must be the answer.

62
00:04:13.685 --> 00:04:18.913
In the full experience, each finished section
also reveals more of the scene.

63
00:04:19.713 --> 00:04:21.249
Stuck? Press Hint.

64
00:04:21.399 --> 00:04:23.640
The first hint points you to a clue.

65
00:04:24.440 --> 00:04:28.558
Press Show more for the exact square, and then
the full reasoning.

66
00:04:28.708 --> 00:04:31.631
You can even let it mark the square for you.

67
00:04:32.431 --> 00:04:36.507
Press Check at any time to see whether any of
your marks are wrong.

68
00:04:37.307 --> 00:04:42.875
Made a mistake? Undo and Redo take back any
move, as many times as you like.

69
00:04:43.675 --> 00:04:48.732
Prefer words to grids? List view lets you
choose each match from a menu.

70
00:04:48.882 --> 00:04:53.107
The game also works fully by keyboard and with
a screen reader.

71
00:04:53.907 --> 00:04:58.985
When you think you know, answer the questions
under the clues, and press Check answers.

72
00:04:59.785 --> 00:05:03.476
Want to jot something down? Press My notes and
type.

73
00:05:03.626 --> 00:05:07.445
Press Save to keep them, or Close to get back
to the puzzle.

74
00:05:07.595 --> 00:05:10.711
Only you can see your notes, even in a race.

75
00:05:11.511 --> 00:05:16.354
Keep going the same way, clue by clue, until
the whole grid is filled in.

76
00:05:17.154 --> 00:05:18.413
Case closed!

77
00:05:18.563 --> 00:05:24.800
Felix arrived at 9:45 PM, so Felix was behind
the ring of keys all along!

78
00:05:24.820 --> 00:05:28.484
It was a prank with a bedsheet and a fan.

79
00:05:28.634 --> 00:05:32.752
You also see your time and a suggestion for
your next puzzle.

80
00:05:33.552 --> 00:05:38.993
Then rate the puzzle, and say whether it felt
too easy, just right or too hard.

81
00:05:39.143 --> 00:05:43.687
The game learns from your answers and tunes
your next puzzle to suit you.

82
00:05:44.487 --> 00:05:50.333
You can print any puzzle, blank or with your
marks, with the answer key on its own page.

83
00:05:51.133 --> 00:05:53.566
Your progress saves automatically.

84
00:05:53.716 --> 00:05:58.303
Come back any time and pick up where you left
off, from Saved puzzles.

85
00:05:59.103 --> 00:06:01.963
Press Help to see every keyboard shortcut.

86
00:06:02.763 --> 00:06:07.265
And How to play, at the top of every page,
plays this video again.

87
00:06:08.065 --> 00:06:10.305
Play in light or dark colors,

88
00:06:11.105 --> 00:06:12.941
or in high contrast.

89
00:06:13.741 --> 00:06:17.901
And Silent mode is always there when you just
want the puzzle.

90
00:06:18.701 --> 00:06:23.459
To play without opening a browser, choose
Install the app from the Menu.

91
00:06:23.609 --> 00:06:27.983
Download the Windows desktop app, which keeps
itself up to date.

92
00:06:28.133 --> 00:06:31.782
Or add the game's icon to your phone's home
screen.

93
00:06:31.802 --> 00:06:35.046
On your phone, the same menu shows you how.

94
00:06:35.846 --> 00:06:38.407
You can also play with other detectives.

95
00:06:39.207 --> 00:06:41.426
You never need an account to play.

96
00:06:41.576 --> 00:06:44.002
But a free account keeps your puzzles,

97
00:06:44.022 --> 00:06:49.129
progress and settings in step on the website,
the desktop app and your phone.

98
00:06:49.929 --> 00:06:52.745
The name at the top shows who you are playing
as.

99
00:06:52.895 --> 00:06:55.605
Until you sign in, you play as Guest.

100
00:06:56.405 --> 00:06:59.201
Create one with your email and a password.

101
00:06:59.351 --> 00:07:03.830
Keep me signed in is ticked, so you stay
signed in on this device.

102
00:07:03.850 --> 00:07:06.114
Untick it on a shared computer.

103
00:07:06.264 --> 00:07:11.363
If you ever forget your password, Forgot
password sends you a reset link.

104
00:07:12.163 --> 00:07:15.812
Once you are signed in, your puzzles sync on
their own.

105
00:07:15.962 --> 00:07:19.717
Sign in on another device and they are waiting
for you.

106
00:07:20.517 --> 00:07:23.675
Once you are signed in, you pick a screen
name.

107
00:07:23.825 --> 00:07:28.562
It is the only thing other players see, and
rude names are turned away.

108
00:07:28.712 --> 00:07:32.467
Don't want one? Sign out instead, and you play
as Guest.

109
00:07:33.267 --> 00:07:35.913
Your screen name now shows at the top.

110
00:07:36.063 --> 00:07:40.889
Play against others lets you race other
players on the very same puzzle,

111
00:07:40.909 --> 00:07:42.741
and climb the scoreboard.

112
00:07:43.541 --> 00:07:45.569
To race, press Start a race.

113
00:07:45.719 --> 00:07:50.967
It uses the difficulty, theme and size you
picked on the New puzzle screen.

114
00:07:51.767 --> 00:07:54.712
Share the race code or link with a friend.

115
00:07:54.862 --> 00:07:58.937
Or anyone can press Find a race to join an
open race.

116
00:07:59.737 --> 00:08:02.319
Everyone gets the very same puzzle.

117
00:08:02.469 --> 00:08:07.185
The race bar shows the code, and Standings
shows who is still solving.

118
00:08:07.985 --> 00:08:10.353
When you finish, you see your place.

119
00:08:10.503 --> 00:08:13.960
Fastest solve wins, and each hint adds time.

120
00:08:14.760 --> 00:08:18.345
The scoreboard ranks players this week and of
all time.

121
00:08:18.495 --> 00:08:22.463
Every solve earns points, even when you play
on your own.

122
00:08:22.613 --> 00:08:27.307
Press Scoring and race rules to see exactly
how points are awarded.

123
00:08:28.107 --> 00:08:32.161
This week's leaders are always in view at the
top of the page.

124
00:08:32.311 --> 00:08:35.064
Select Scoreboard there to see the full board.

125
00:08:35.864 --> 00:08:41.091
To race one particular player, press Challenge
a player and type their screen name.

126
00:08:41.891 --> 00:08:47.225
They see your challenge under Play against
others, the next time they open the game.

127
00:08:47.375 --> 00:08:52.624
Accept starts the race on the very same
puzzle. No thanks turns it down.

128
00:08:53.424 --> 00:08:55.601
Finally, make the game your own.

129
00:08:56.401 --> 00:09:02.289
In Settings, sound effects and theme music
start on, and you can turn either one off.

130
00:09:02.439 --> 00:09:06.088
Learn from how I play tunes your next puzzles
to suit you.

131
00:09:06.888 --> 00:09:10.345
Have an idea for a story, or found a problem?

132
00:09:10.495 --> 00:09:14.585
Ideas and problems, in the menu, has a
separate box for each,

133
00:09:14.605 --> 00:09:17.450
and they go straight to the game's team.

134
00:09:18.250 --> 00:09:23.989
That's all you need: read the story, follow
the clues, and mark your X's and O's.

135
00:09:24.139 --> 00:09:28.343
Welcome to The Fantastical Logic Grid. Happy
sleuthing!

